<p>President Trump said May 1 that the United States will raise tariffs on cars and trucks imported from the European Union to 25% next week, accusing the bloc of not complying with a trade deal reached last year. He did not specify the alleged breach in his social media post, but told reporters the higher duty would push European automakers to move production to U.S. plants more quickly. The 2025 U.S.-EU trade framework, reached by Trump and European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen last July, capped U.S. tariffs on EU autos and parts at 15%. Politico reported that the agreement required the EU to lower tariff rates on U.S. industrial goods, buy $750 billion worth of energy and invest $600 billion in exchange for lower U.S. tariff rates. Pakistan Today reported that EU officials criticized the move as arbitrary and warned of a firm response.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/gXd5OjCwp9Mb_In8ze6Bx6PyximwmBp3XJFEQOFlUb0XC096i7k33s0bjFcbKpIyleiA4gurb2pZr7WT--IIwJWQGondn1gj0X9mw31eS25HyRxJGRMf1-JpaawGBt363PpcqNFBU0njxizsNf0Rbt48zNz4rzcCwG8dvIfZiThxfmsc15u-jyc8oLPcsgiU2pCZwBL7ZBx5YMu7kH9VT239iMVNmjUmZl-VYbouyJ7ux78NA5nuKfq0PC5uCriEXUXdclHwu449uVs2Gw' alt='A worker performs final checks on the Volkswagen electric car factory floor in Emden, Germany, in February.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Legal backdrop: A 2026 Supreme Court ruling struck down Trump&#x27;s authority for some global levies, but AFP reported that sector-specific auto duties were not affected.</li><li>Ratification status: RT reported that EU lawmakers had not fully ratified the U.S.-EU deal agreed last July.</li></ul><blockquote>It is fully understood and agreed that, if they produce Cars and Trucks in U.S.A. Plants, there will be NO TARIFF. - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>European economist: Pakistan Today reported that one European economist urged Brussels and Berlin to &quot;finally show some backbone&quot; by imposing retaliatory tariffs. (<a hr